# Merge behaviour for this repository's shared append-only registries.
# The kit's template, applied to the repository that ships it —
# see starter-kit/gitattributes.template for the full reasoning.

# Generated artifact: the [Unreleased] section is assembled from changelog.d/.
# `merge=union` is safe here only because check-registry-drift.sh runs in CI and
# rejects any artifact that stopped matching its fragments. If that check ever
# leaves the lint target, this line goes with it.
CHANGELOG.md          merge=union linguist-generated=true

# Fragments are one file per entry, so two branches add two different paths and
# git merges them without being asked. Stated explicitly: an absent entry would
# read as an oversight rather than a decision.
changelog.d/**        -merge

# Decision records are already one file per decision. The file cannot conflict;
# only the allocated number can, which is what check-registry-ids.sh is for.
docs/adr/**           -merge
